One way to expel disabled people from society would be to limit access to transportation, housing and education. Disabled people often require additional support and resources which could strain these already limited systems and thus prove financially costly. Additionally, many people have a ableist attitude towards disabled individuals which makes it difficult for them to gain employment and become contributing members of society. Further, many buildings, services and activities are inaccessible or designed without consideration for disabled individuals making it hard for them participate in day-to-day life. Excluding disabled people from school can also rob them of the opportunity to develop their skills further adding insult to injury.
So essentially we can exile disabled individuals by ensuring that our society remains hostile towards them by providing physical barriers that prevent access as well as economic/financial barriers by making education, employment opportunities & resources limited or simply unavailable.
